cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite both the paper and the archived
  release.
title: >-
  HTN Planning as a Coordination Layer for Multi-Server MCP Tool
  Orchestration — Artifact: GTPyhop planning, JSON binding, and a
  cross-server MCP orchestration middleware
abstract: >-
  Research artifact for the HPlan workshop paper "HTN Planning as a
  Coordination Layer for Multi-Server MCP Tool Orchestration" (ICAPS 2026,
  Dublin). Reproduces the planning layer for the paper's five HTN domains,
  the planner -> JSON binding -> orchestration middleware pipeline offline
  with no database, and the live drug-target-discovery run against the eight
  Augmented Nature MCP servers, together with the original log of the three
  live runs reported in the paper.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
# NOTE: CFF permits one licence field. The repository is mixed-licence --
